From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:21:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] migration/savevm: reset load_section_id at the start of
 qemu_loadvm_state

A part or end section names its handler by the section id that the
stream's full or start section gave it, and the lookup takes the first
handler whose load_section_id matches. Nothing ever cleared those ids,
so after one load a second load in the same process can match a handler
by an id from the earlier stream: whenever the two streams were saved
with a different device order, the section goes to the wrong handler.

Seen on pseries: loadvm of an image snapshot saved without an extra
spapr-vscsi, then savevm and loadvm in the extended config. The second
stream's spapr/htab part section went to xhci (the id it had in the
first stream), and the load failed with "Invalid value -1 expecting
positive value <= 2" in the PCI device state. Record/replay hits this
on every begin, since it saves and reloads its start snapshot right
after the image's snapshot was loaded.

Forget the ids before reading a new stream.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

Origin: new
---
 migration/savevm.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/migration/savevm.c b/migration/savevm.c
index fb4285ae8b60283c273e63269368d188b7a6ea56..4583c2ae8982753c29932604a12b30871f1a248b 100644
--- a/migration/savevm.c
+++ b/migration/savevm.c
@@ -3092,6 +3092,7 @@ int qemu_loadvm_state(QEMUFile *f, Error **errp)
     MigrationState *s = migrate_get_current();
     MigrationIncomingState *mis = migration_incoming_get_current();
     int ret;
+    SaveStateEntry *se;
 
     if (qemu_savevm_state_blocked(errp)) {
         return -EINVAL;
@@ -3099,6 +3100,15 @@ int qemu_loadvm_state(QEMUFile *f, Error **errp)
 
     qemu_loadvm_thread_pool_create(mis);
 
+    /*
+     * Section ids belong to the stream being loaded: forget the previous
+     * load's, or a part/end section matches the first handler that had
+     * this id in an earlier stream saved with a different device order.
+     */
+    QTAILQ_FOREACH(se, &savevm_state.handlers, entry) {
+        se->load_section_id = -1;
+    }
+
     ret = qemu_loadvm_state_header(f, errp);
     if (ret) {
         return ret;
